        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "6719cb6b-8276-5688-8e57-7de0f435f93d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Pal Dukagjini, Nicholas Dukagjini, Skanderbeg, George Castriot\n- Organizations: League of Lezhë, Ottoman Empire, Republic of Venice, Kingdom of Naples\n- Roles: Albanian nobleman, military commander\n- Topics: Albanian liberation\n\nFacts:\n- George Castriot, known as Skanderbeg, was born on 6 May 1405 and died on 17 January 1468.\n- Skanderbeg was an Albanian nobleman and military commander.\n- Skanderbeg served the Ottoman Empire from 1423 to 1443.\n- The League of Lezhë was a military alliance founded by Skanderbeg that sought the liberation of Albania from the Ottoman Empire.\n- Skanderbeg served the Republic of Venice from 1443 to 1447.\n- Pal Dukagjini and Nicholas Dukagjini were part of the League of Lezhë.\n- Skanderbeg served the Kingdom of Naples until his death.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "91a3a9c7-158c-5811-99a7-fa96edafcd10",
        "text": "Page: Pal Dukagjini. Sentence: Pal and Nicholas were part of the League of Lezhë, a military alliance that sought liberation of Albania from the Ottoman Empire, founded by the powerful Skanderbeg.\nPage: Skanderbeg. Sentence: George Castriot (Albanian: \"Gjergj Kastrioti\" , 6 May 1405 – 17 January 1468), known as Skanderbeg (Albanian: \"Skënderbej or Skënderbeu\" from Ottoman Turkish: اسکندر بگ‎ \"İskender Bey\"), was an Albanian nobleman and military commander, who served the Ottoman Empire in 1423–43, the Republic of Venice in 1443–47, and lastly the Kingdom of Naples until his death.",
